1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,060
[Disclaimer: This series is created
solely for entertainment purposes.

2
00:00:01,080 --> 00:00:02,330
All individuals, behaviors, places,
and events depicted are entirely fictional,

3
00:00:02,350 --> 00:00:05,000
with no intention to represent or reference any
organizations, departments, occupations, or individuals]

4
00:00:05,020 --> 00:00:06,800
Whoever dares to take
Chris away from me

5
00:00:06,890 --> 00:00:07,960
will die.

6
00:00:07,980 --> 00:00:09,580
What did she do

7
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:11,930
to make you like her so much
that you stayed with her all night?!

8
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:13,610
Let's not be together.

9
00:00:13,790 --> 00:00:15,440
It really isn't going to work out.

10
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:17,590
Can you not disappear like that again?

11
00:00:17,630 --> 00:00:19,040
If you don't want me to disappear,

12
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:21,600
make me yours, then.

13
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:36,000
Sun...

14
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:37,900
Sun?

15
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:57,390
I'm going out to get some food.

16
00:00:57,730 --> 00:00:59,200
I'll come back and make it up to you.

17
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,080
[Nadear's father]

18
00:01:31,150 --> 00:01:32,000
Yes, Dad?

19
00:01:33,390 --> 00:01:34,600
Where have you been?

20
00:01:34,830 --> 00:01:37,080
Why did you leave Nadear
alone in the hospital?

21
00:01:37,620 --> 00:01:39,190
Was she sick?

22
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:41,480
Do you still have the audacity to ask me that?

23
00:01:43,180 --> 00:01:44,680
Calm down, dear.

24
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:06,100
[Third Person]

25
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:17,630
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

26
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:23,310
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

27
00:02:23,340 --> 00:02:26,950
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

28
00:02:27,680 --> 00:02:33,370
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

29
00:02:33,390 --> 00:02:42,820
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

30
00:02:43,220 --> 00:02:48,270
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

31
00:02:48,290 --> 00:02:52,570
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

32
00:02:52,590 --> 00:03:01,510
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

33
00:03:01,980 --> 00:03:10,110
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

34
00:03:29,890 --> 00:03:30,600
Chris,

35
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:32,210
shall we have breakfast?

36
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:50,440
Sun.

37
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:53,280
Chris...

38
00:03:53,610 --> 00:03:54,610
What's wrong?

39
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:57,190
Why are you crying?

40
00:03:58,310 --> 00:04:00,510
I thought you left me.

41
00:04:04,520 --> 00:04:05,460
Poor thing.

42
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:07,080
How could I abandon you?

43
00:04:08,210 --> 00:04:10,110
I just went downstairs to look for you.

44
00:04:12,490 --> 00:04:14,280
Why did you disappear

45
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:15,760
without leaving me a note?

46
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:18,160
You scared me to death, you know that?

47
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:20,600
Aw...

48
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:22,920
I'm right here now, my love.

49
00:04:24,780 --> 00:04:25,710
I have something for you, too.

50
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:30,200
Here.

51
00:04:31,500 --> 00:04:32,500
Cute.

52
00:04:36,290 --> 00:04:37,520
This is just temporary.

53
00:04:38,220 --> 00:04:40,090
When I'm ready to give
you the real thing,

54
00:04:40,110 --> 00:04:41,280
I'll come back and propose.

55
00:04:44,310 --> 00:04:46,080
No taking it back once you've promised.

56
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:54,200
It's only been one night,

57
00:04:54,220 --> 00:04:55,320
and you want to get engaged?

58
00:04:58,500 --> 00:05:00,090
Aren't you a little too easy?

59
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:03,900
I might be,

60
00:05:04,520 --> 00:05:06,280
but only for you, Sun.

61
00:05:08,980 --> 00:05:12,000
Because you're the only person
who makes me feel the love,

62
00:05:12,810 --> 00:05:14,520
and feel loved in return.

63
00:05:22,010 --> 00:05:24,090
You're the only person for me too.

64
00:05:33,620 --> 00:05:35,300
Shall we go swimming

65
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:36,320
after breakfast?

66
00:05:40,310 --> 00:05:41,310
I'm sorry.

67
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:44,760
But I have to leave.

68
00:05:57,610 --> 00:05:59,700
To be honest, I don't want to go back yet,

69
00:06:00,220 --> 00:06:01,810
but Nadear is sick.

70
00:06:01,830 --> 00:06:03,200
There's no one to take care of her.

71
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:07,200
Nadear always took care of me
whenever I was sick.

72
00:06:10,670 --> 00:06:11,670
You should go.

73
00:06:12,460 --> 00:06:13,590
I understand.

74
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:18,300
But...

75
00:06:18,590 --> 00:06:20,600
You can trust me.

76
00:06:21,210 --> 00:06:23,700
Nadear is just a friend.

77
00:06:25,400 --> 00:06:27,600
But you and I are...

78
00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:29,640
What are we?

79
00:06:31,510 --> 00:06:32,520
"Wives."

80
00:06:33,470 --> 00:06:34,510
No way.

81
00:06:34,770 --> 00:06:35,670
"Husbands?"

82
00:06:35,690 --> 00:06:37,080
Are you crazy?

83
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:39,800
Why don't we become girlfriends first?

84
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:44,000
We'll be that soon enough. Just you wait.

85
00:06:46,900 --> 00:06:47,580
Oh!

86
00:06:48,110 --> 00:06:49,300
I have something for you.

87
00:06:51,800 --> 00:06:52,510
Here.

88
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:55,040
You can stop by if you miss me.

89
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:58,410
You said I'm easy,

90
00:06:58,730 --> 00:07:01,300
but giving me your condo keycard
isn't being easy at all?

91
00:07:01,910 --> 00:07:04,300
Well, everything else is already hard enough.

92
00:07:16,610 --> 00:07:19,570
The doctor said she had
intestinal inflammation from food poisoning.

93
00:07:19,590 --> 00:07:22,830
She's been given antibiotics,
so she should feel better soon.

94
00:07:23,230 --> 00:07:24,760
And once her IV runs out,

95
00:07:24,790 --> 00:07:26,560
she can go home.

96
00:07:26,800 --> 00:07:28,910
Dad, Mom, don't worry, okay?

97
00:07:29,710 --> 00:07:31,500
Chris can take care of me.

98
00:07:34,100 --> 00:07:35,030
Okay.

99
00:07:35,260 --> 00:07:37,400
How? She was gone all night.

100
00:07:38,210 --> 00:07:39,070
Come on...

101
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:42,440
Please, don't say that to her.

102
00:07:42,590 --> 00:07:45,300
She went out to look for ideas
for the new dishes.

103
00:07:46,510 --> 00:07:47,790
That's why she was busy.

104
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:50,500
It's also my fault for not
being careful about what I ate.

105
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:52,820
Hey,

106
00:07:52,910 --> 00:07:54,830
how many times have I told you

107
00:07:54,850 --> 00:07:57,340
that you've had a weak stomach
since you were little?

108
00:07:57,360 --> 00:08:00,080
Eating something strange can
give you a stomachache.

109
00:08:00,300 --> 00:08:01,740
For now,

110
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:04,320
you need to find something light
for Nadear to eat, okay?

111
00:08:05,490 --> 00:08:06,490
Yes, Mom.

112
00:08:07,200 --> 00:08:08,000
Hey, Chris,

113
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:10,190
take care of Nadear, okay?

114
00:08:12,490 --> 00:08:13,550
If you leave her

115
00:08:13,630 --> 00:08:14,810
this time,

116
00:08:15,260 --> 00:08:16,610
I won't forgive you.

117
00:08:16,640 --> 00:08:18,200
Come on now, dear.

118
00:08:18,340 --> 00:08:20,100
What are you even saying?

119
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:28,190
You don't have to take that to heart.

120
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:31,090
I won't.

121
00:08:31,910 --> 00:08:34,590
I understand that
your parents are worried about you.

122
00:08:36,300 --> 00:08:38,190
Once you get better,

123
00:08:38,490 --> 00:08:41,280
I'll tell them that we
broke up a long time ago.

124
00:08:41,890 --> 00:08:42,890
You can't do that!

125
00:08:44,620 --> 00:08:47,830
You promised me
you'd stay with me for two more months.

126
00:08:49,860 --> 00:08:51,760
I want to take back that promise.

127
00:08:53,190 --> 00:08:55,200
But it's just two more months.

128
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:57,850
Can't you hold on a little longer?

129
00:08:58,480 --> 00:09:00,710
And I'll give you

130
00:09:01,190 --> 00:09:02,630
the rest of your life back.

131
00:09:04,100 --> 00:09:06,900
This is the last time

132
00:09:07,310 --> 00:09:09,220
I'll ask you for a favor.

133
00:09:15,070 --> 00:09:15,790
Alright.

134
00:09:16,660 --> 00:09:18,580
If you want two more months,

135
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:20,090
I'll give you that.

136
00:09:20,470 --> 00:09:22,800
But only as your friend.

137
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:25,490
Just like I'm doing right now.

138
00:09:26,010 --> 00:09:27,130
When a friend gets sick,

139
00:09:27,990 --> 00:09:29,230
I'll come to take care of them.

140
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:34,800
This is the first time

141
00:09:35,900 --> 00:09:38,130
I don't want to feel better.

142
00:09:39,900 --> 00:09:42,020
But I want to see my friend healthy and strong.

143
00:10:12,340 --> 00:10:14,090
I brought you your food and medicine.

144
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:16,490
Get some rest after you eat, okay?

145
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:20,810
I'm heading outside for a bit.

146
00:10:22,620 --> 00:10:24,010
Will you be back late?

147
00:10:27,250 --> 00:10:29,120
I'm not going to complain.

148
00:10:29,510 --> 00:10:32,810
Mom and Dad said they'll call me.

149
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:36,580
I'm worried that if they don't see you,

150
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:38,500
they'll come all the way here.

151
00:10:39,810 --> 00:10:42,590
Can you come back and
talk to my parents?

152
00:10:44,590 --> 00:10:45,590
Of course.

153
00:10:45,620 --> 00:10:47,210
Since my friend asked,
of course I'll do it.

154
00:10:48,020 --> 00:10:49,520
Don't forget to eat and take your meds.

155
00:11:05,830 --> 00:11:07,620
Surprise!

156
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:21,600
Don't you have someone sick to take care of?

157
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:25,610
Well, I need some time off, too.

158
00:11:25,850 --> 00:11:27,550
I'll go back tonight.

159
00:11:30,130 --> 00:11:31,490
Here.

160
00:11:31,670 --> 00:11:33,340
I got these for you.

161
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:49,200
You remembered...?

162
00:11:51,540 --> 00:11:52,790
Remember what?

163
00:11:54,220 --> 00:11:56,100
Why did you buy me cheesecake?

164
00:11:58,180 --> 00:11:59,300
I didn't mean anything by it.

165
00:11:59,710 --> 00:12:01,120
I just thought it looked appetizing.

166
00:12:05,890 --> 00:12:06,900
You did.

167
00:12:07,920 --> 00:12:09,320
You just don't realize that.

168
00:12:22,960 --> 00:12:23,820
How is it?

169
00:12:26,700 --> 00:12:27,340
Amazing.

170
00:12:29,300 --> 00:12:30,300
Can you feed me too?

171
00:12:36,470 --> 00:12:37,470
Oh!

172
00:12:38,490 --> 00:12:39,520
Sun!

173
00:12:39,540 --> 00:12:40,900
Don't waste it like that.

174
00:12:48,710 --> 00:12:49,780
It's not a waste anymore.

175
00:13:01,110 --> 00:13:02,110
Chris...

176
00:13:02,420 --> 00:13:03,420
Me too.

177
00:13:18,690 --> 00:13:20,010
When do you have to go back?

178
00:13:21,720 --> 00:13:22,720
Not right now.

179
00:13:25,210 --> 00:13:27,210
Can I get my fill of you for now?

180
00:13:38,300 --> 00:13:47,920
♫I'm missing all those times you were mine,♫

181
00:13:47,940 --> 00:13:52,900
♫But I understand when love runs out of time♫

182
00:13:52,920 --> 00:13:57,190
♫I'm no longer the muse inside your heart,♫

183
00:13:57,210 --> 00:14:03,080
♫So I'm willing to step away and depart♫

184
00:14:03,100 --> 00:14:12,850
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

185
00:14:12,900 --> 00:14:17,910
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

186
00:14:17,930 --> 00:14:22,150
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

187
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:30,840
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

188
00:14:31,560 --> 00:14:39,810
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

189
00:14:58,610 --> 00:14:59,520
Chris,

190
00:15:01,570 --> 00:15:02,490
wake up.

191
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:04,480
It's late.

192
00:15:05,020 --> 00:15:06,320
Don't you have to go home?

193
00:15:08,450 --> 00:15:10,220
I'm still sleepy...

194
00:15:10,800 --> 00:15:12,390
Just a bit longer...

195
00:15:52,220 --> 00:15:54,950
[Third Person]

196
00:15:56,136 --> 00:16:00,006
[Third Person]

197
00:16:27,226 --> 00:16:28,916
You were so stubborn last night.

198
00:16:29,516 --> 00:16:31,016
You refused to get up.

199
00:16:32,566 --> 00:16:33,916
Well, I was tired.

200
00:16:36,016 --> 00:16:37,426
Don't give me that.

201
00:16:41,086 --> 00:16:43,826
I didn't think I'd sleep that long, either.

202
00:16:44,926 --> 00:16:47,096
I actually have a really
hard time falling asleep.

203
00:16:47,626 --> 00:16:49,306
But when I'm with you,

204
00:16:49,496 --> 00:16:51,106
I always fall asleep so easily.

205
00:16:54,156 --> 00:16:55,816
Are you some kind of sleeping pill?

206
00:17:00,576 --> 00:17:02,226
Since when did you have trouble sleeping?

207
00:17:06,246 --> 00:17:08,226
Ever since I lost my memories,

208
00:17:09,186 --> 00:17:10,526
I've had to rely on sleeping pills.

209
00:17:16,986 --> 00:17:18,006
I'm sorry.

210
00:17:22,326 --> 00:17:23,826
Why are you apologizing?

211
00:17:26,756 --> 00:17:28,626
You talk as if...

212
00:17:29,576 --> 00:17:31,336
we know each other again.

213
00:17:33,406 --> 00:17:35,216
Is there anything you want to tell me?

214
00:17:41,556 --> 00:17:43,456
I'll tell you when the time is right.

215
00:17:44,506 --> 00:17:45,926
But for now, you should go back.

216
00:17:48,916 --> 00:17:50,746
Don't forget to apologize to her, too.

217
00:17:54,616 --> 00:17:56,516
You're not jealous,

218
00:17:57,126 --> 00:17:58,606
and you're worried about her too?

219
00:18:00,206 --> 00:18:01,526
How nice of you.

220
00:18:05,016 --> 00:18:06,626
I'm not a good person.

221
00:18:08,816 --> 00:18:10,606
But I'm thankful

222
00:18:11,306 --> 00:18:13,026
that she took care of you.

223
00:18:17,276 --> 00:18:18,906
What a saint.

224
00:18:21,286 --> 00:18:22,416
It's nothing like that.

225
00:18:27,806 --> 00:18:29,106
I'm not a good person.

226
00:18:30,966 --> 00:18:33,616
If you knew what I've done,

227
00:18:35,076 --> 00:18:37,306
you might not love me anymore.

228
00:19:00,766 --> 00:19:01,626
Chris?

229
00:19:07,206 --> 00:19:08,816
The past is in the past.

230
00:19:10,296 --> 00:19:12,216
Right now, I love you.

231
00:19:13,566 --> 00:19:14,716
And I won't stop loving you.

232
00:19:54,226 --> 00:19:55,366
You're back?

233
00:19:55,386 --> 00:19:57,356
Come have breakfast.
I ordered this for you.

234
00:20:03,526 --> 00:20:04,576
Aren't you angry?

235
00:20:08,186 --> 00:20:09,516
I'm more scared.

236
00:20:11,616 --> 00:20:14,036
If I got angry and you never come back,

237
00:20:14,056 --> 00:20:15,316
what would I do then?

238
00:20:22,426 --> 00:20:23,516
I'm sorry.

239
00:20:25,066 --> 00:20:27,016
Did your parents call you last night?

240
00:20:31,136 --> 00:20:32,206
They did...

241
00:20:33,426 --> 00:20:35,606
But I told them you were sleeping.

242
00:20:36,676 --> 00:20:38,516
They'll probably call me again today.

243
00:20:44,116 --> 00:20:45,636
But don't worry,

244
00:20:46,576 --> 00:20:47,826
it might be better to let them

245
00:20:47,846 --> 00:20:50,226
slowly get used to not seeing you...

246
00:21:00,636 --> 00:21:01,716
Oh, Chris,

247
00:21:02,116 --> 00:21:04,676
Nan admitted that she'd embezzled
money from our restaurant.

248
00:21:06,526 --> 00:21:07,526
Why did she do that?

249
00:21:09,626 --> 00:21:12,316
She was struggling financially,
so she used the money to pay her mortgage.

250
00:21:12,606 --> 00:21:15,026
But she promised she wouldn't do it again.

251
00:21:15,636 --> 00:21:18,536
And she'll pay back all
the money she took.

252
00:21:19,226 --> 00:21:21,716
She only asks to be allowed
to keep working at this restaurant.

253
00:21:23,856 --> 00:21:25,126
Is that really okay, Nadear?

254
00:21:27,416 --> 00:21:29,606
Can you give her another chance?

255
00:21:31,756 --> 00:21:35,306
When I left work to take care
of you, Nan was the one who

256
00:21:35,326 --> 00:21:36,926
took care of our restaurant.

257
00:21:38,516 --> 00:21:40,916
That's why she embezzled money from us, too.

258
00:21:41,616 --> 00:21:43,716
I'll keep an eye on her.

259
00:21:45,066 --> 00:21:47,316
But wasn't Nan able to embezzle money

260
00:21:47,626 --> 00:21:49,646
under your watch?

261
00:21:50,016 --> 00:21:52,516
If you don't trust me,

262
00:21:54,186 --> 00:21:56,706
will you keep an eye on her yourself, then?

263
00:22:00,236 --> 00:22:01,236
Of course,

264
00:22:01,716 --> 00:22:02,716
I'll do it myself.

265
00:22:06,916 --> 00:22:10,976
[Third Person
Bar - Bistro]

266
00:22:16,196 --> 00:22:17,226
Wawah.

267
00:22:17,526 --> 00:22:18,616
Are you short on cash lately?

268
00:22:22,476 --> 00:22:23,976
Would you like to earn some extra money?

269
00:22:29,036 --> 00:22:30,896
Did you bring everything?

270
00:22:31,726 --> 00:22:32,906
This one seems broken?

271
00:22:33,416 --> 00:22:34,596
Please sign for your delivery.

272
00:22:37,056 --> 00:22:38,426
Let me do that for you.

273
00:22:43,226 --> 00:22:44,706
Wawah, help me check the items.

274
00:22:49,836 --> 00:22:50,816
Wawah,

275
00:22:50,836 --> 00:22:52,216
go sort out the stock inside.

276
00:22:52,406 --> 00:22:54,096
Let me handle these.

277
00:22:54,726 --> 00:22:57,216
I usually do it by myself anyway.

278
00:22:57,616 --> 00:22:58,616
It's alright, Nan.

279
00:22:58,646 --> 00:23:01,516
Wawah and I will double-check
everything this time,

280
00:23:01,656 --> 00:23:03,116
so nothing goes missing.

281
00:23:04,136 --> 00:23:04,726
Oh, and...

282
00:23:04,746 --> 00:23:07,316
from now on, if you're going to
order anything or request stock,

283
00:23:08,156 --> 00:23:09,976
please let me check it first.

284
00:23:12,246 --> 00:23:13,246
Sure thing.

285
00:23:13,676 --> 00:23:17,186
I'm glad you're finally...

286
00:23:17,206 --> 00:23:19,376
able to do your job like
the other shareholders again.

287
00:23:36,456 --> 00:23:37,456
Here.

288
00:24:20,446 --> 00:24:21,856
I'm hungry.

289
00:24:25,416 --> 00:24:27,326
Come over, then.

290
00:24:27,406 --> 00:24:29,336
You haven't tasted this in a while.

291
00:24:36,896 --> 00:24:38,836
I really want to go,

292
00:24:38,856 --> 00:24:40,256
but I have so much work.

293
00:24:57,096 --> 00:24:59,416
Come over when you're done working, okay?

294
00:25:00,926 --> 00:25:01,766
Oops!

295
00:25:27,816 --> 00:25:30,336
[I missed you]

296
00:25:42,696 --> 00:25:44,226
Is she really not going to reply?

297
00:25:44,266 --> 00:25:45,706
Did work kill her or something?

298
00:25:50,926 --> 00:25:51,586
Chris!

299
00:25:52,036 --> 00:25:54,636
I missed you too.

300
00:25:59,236 --> 00:26:00,606
I came here as soon as I got your message.

301
00:26:00,626 --> 00:26:01,706
I even forgot to bring my phone.

302
00:26:01,726 --> 00:26:03,216
I thought it was in my pocket.

303
00:26:04,056 --> 00:26:06,306
You came all this way just to reply to me?

304
00:26:09,336 --> 00:26:10,766
I came to have a taste, too.

305
00:26:22,736 --> 00:26:23,576
[Third Person
Bar - Bistro]

306
00:26:23,596 --> 00:26:25,176
If your girlfriend keeps
checking up on me like this,

307
00:26:25,196 --> 00:26:26,196
I can't stand it.

308
00:26:28,416 --> 00:26:31,726
Do you expect Chris to be happy
that you embezzled money, then?

309
00:26:31,916 --> 00:26:32,896
That's not how it works.

310
00:26:33,916 --> 00:26:36,006
If you want to keep working here,

311
00:26:36,356 --> 00:26:37,816
you'll have to put up with it.

312
00:26:38,776 --> 00:26:40,026
You know full well

313
00:26:40,046 --> 00:26:41,686
why things are still this way.

314
00:26:43,116 --> 00:26:44,786
Find a way to fix this.

315
00:26:44,816 --> 00:26:46,496
Stop her from pestering me.

316
00:26:46,836 --> 00:26:48,576
And what am I supposed to do?

317
00:26:48,926 --> 00:26:50,726
If you can't think of a way to fix this,

318
00:26:51,316 --> 00:26:54,696
should I have her start
checking up on you instead?

319
00:27:19,676 --> 00:27:21,506
Thank you for coming to see me.

320
00:27:33,456 --> 00:27:36,966
How am I supposed to bear watching
someone I love be with someone else?

321
00:27:38,116 --> 00:27:39,326
What else can you do

322
00:27:40,696 --> 00:27:42,226
but bear it?

323
00:27:43,386 --> 00:27:45,106
I don't want to bear it.

324
00:27:46,326 --> 00:27:48,216
I loved her first.

325
00:27:49,116 --> 00:27:51,116
I want her back.

326
00:27:51,656 --> 00:27:52,916
We...

327
00:27:53,626 --> 00:27:55,846
can't always get what we want, Nadear.

328
00:27:56,196 --> 00:27:58,496
Are you a walking quote or something?

329
00:27:59,536 --> 00:28:00,606
I know

330
00:28:00,856 --> 00:28:03,126
we can't always get what we want,

331
00:28:03,916 --> 00:28:06,136
but I only want Chris.

332
00:28:06,816 --> 00:28:07,976
She should be mine.

333
00:28:08,126 --> 00:28:09,616
Just let Chris go, Nadear.

334
00:28:10,026 --> 00:28:11,456
Chris doesn't love you.

335
00:28:12,056 --> 00:28:14,406
- Chris loves...
- Don't you dare say her name!

336
00:28:15,316 --> 00:28:16,706
Chris doesn't love her!

337
00:28:16,806 --> 00:28:18,606
She is just misguided.

338
00:28:19,186 --> 00:28:21,236
She did all those things to her.

339
00:28:21,256 --> 00:28:23,536
How could Chris possibly love her?!

340
00:28:24,826 --> 00:28:25,826
Nadear,

341
00:28:26,136 --> 00:28:27,136
let go.

342
00:28:30,066 --> 00:28:31,916
Chris has to love me.

343
00:28:34,516 --> 00:28:36,346
You saw it too.

344
00:28:37,566 --> 00:28:39,626
I did everything for her.

345
00:28:47,606 --> 00:28:49,746
I won't let her leave me.

346
00:28:52,826 --> 00:28:54,726
I'll make her mine.

347
00:28:57,336 --> 00:28:59,106
[Verity Skin Clinic]

348
00:29:02,896 --> 00:29:03,606
Hey,

349
00:29:03,826 --> 00:29:04,916
what should we eat today?

350
00:29:05,826 --> 00:29:06,626
Noodles?

351
00:29:08,186 --> 00:29:08,896
Yeah.

352
00:29:08,976 --> 00:29:11,916
[Verity Skin Clinic]

353
00:29:11,956 --> 00:29:13,806
There's a delivery for Ms. Sun.

354
00:29:16,916 --> 00:29:17,986
From who?

355
00:29:18,016 --> 00:29:19,606
They didn't say anything.

356
00:29:23,236 --> 00:29:24,236
Thank you.

357
00:29:28,706 --> 00:29:30,816
Aren't there any cards at all?

358
00:29:32,626 --> 00:29:34,776
Maybe Chris wanted to surprise me.

359
00:29:36,516 --> 00:29:38,496
It could be someone else, too.

360
00:29:38,526 --> 00:29:40,496
Those puppies and wolves

361
00:29:40,516 --> 00:29:43,236
who like to flirt with you in your DMs.

362
00:29:44,366 --> 00:29:45,606
Those people don't know

363
00:29:45,626 --> 00:29:46,816
what I like.

364
00:29:48,826 --> 00:29:50,716
Only Chris knows that.

365
00:29:51,956 --> 00:29:52,756
Yeah.

366
00:30:00,016 --> 00:30:02,306
The files documenting all the money
Nan embezzled from the restaurant

367
00:30:02,326 --> 00:30:03,406
are here.

368
00:30:05,126 --> 00:30:06,916
She really made two versions of the bills,

369
00:30:06,946 --> 00:30:09,216
just as you suspected.

370
00:30:09,236 --> 00:30:10,406
That's not nice.

371
00:30:12,616 --> 00:30:14,536
Thank you so much for helping me, Wawah.

372
00:30:14,556 --> 00:30:16,116
I'll handle the rest.

373
00:30:16,136 --> 00:30:17,206
You should get back to work.

374
00:30:18,016 --> 00:30:20,226
Just let me know if you need any help.

375
00:30:20,246 --> 00:30:22,216
I love this restaurant too.

376
00:30:23,406 --> 00:30:25,366
I don't know how Nan could do that.

377
00:30:25,706 --> 00:30:27,626
Doesn't she feel bad for Nadear?

378
00:30:27,646 --> 00:30:29,606
She is so frugal.

379
00:30:29,816 --> 00:30:32,736
I even saw Nadear taking
spoiled milk home once.

380
00:30:34,616 --> 00:30:36,606
Probably for watering her plants.

381
00:30:37,636 --> 00:30:38,636
Wait,

382
00:30:39,596 --> 00:30:41,296
when did Nadear take spoiled milk home?

383
00:30:45,926 --> 00:30:47,746
I think...

384
00:30:48,286 --> 00:30:50,126
it was the day before she took sick leave.

385
00:30:50,636 --> 00:30:51,736
Why?

386
00:30:54,416 --> 00:30:55,416
It's nothing.

387
00:30:55,636 --> 00:30:56,736
You can get back to work.

388
00:30:57,526 --> 00:30:58,226
Yes.

389
00:31:12,916 --> 00:31:15,216
Thanks for sending me this.

390
00:31:17,726 --> 00:31:18,496
Should I eat it?

391
00:31:19,816 --> 00:31:21,816
Go ahead and clog your arteries.

392
00:31:33,076 --> 00:31:34,256
Don't eat that cake, Sun.

393
00:31:35,016 --> 00:31:36,016
Why?

394
00:31:36,176 --> 00:31:37,096
I'll tell you later.

395
00:31:37,216 --> 00:31:38,616
Keep that cake.

396
00:31:38,816 --> 00:31:40,496
And don't eat it, no matter what.

397
00:31:46,706 --> 00:31:49,416
[Third Person]

398
00:31:50,606 --> 00:31:54,476
[Third Person]

399
00:32:00,536 --> 00:32:01,266
Chris,

400
00:32:01,806 --> 00:32:02,806
we have to talk.

401
00:32:03,076 --> 00:32:04,386
Not now, Nan.

402
00:32:04,606 --> 00:32:05,556
We have to talk now.

403
00:32:06,646 --> 00:32:07,886
You changed the restaurant's password.

404
00:32:07,906 --> 00:32:09,476
Why didn't you let me access
the restaurant's accounts?

405
00:32:13,156 --> 00:32:14,756
Then why did you steal money
from the restaurant?

406
00:32:18,896 --> 00:32:20,376
I already told you I'd pay it back.

407
00:32:20,396 --> 00:32:21,876
Is it that hard to understand?

408
00:32:22,136 --> 00:32:22,966
Give me the password.

409
00:32:24,076 --> 00:32:25,466
You're the one who doesn't understand.

410
00:32:25,776 --> 00:32:26,816
Didn't you say you wouldn't do it again?

411
00:32:26,836 --> 00:32:28,046
Yet you're still doing it.

412
00:32:28,476 --> 00:32:30,176
Do you think I'm that stupid?

413
00:32:31,296 --> 00:32:33,166
I just borrowed a little money.

414
00:32:33,456 --> 00:32:34,276
What's the big deal?

415
00:32:35,416 --> 00:32:37,406
You never used to speak up like this before.

416
00:32:38,776 --> 00:32:40,476
I'm your goddamn senior.

417
00:32:43,286 --> 00:32:45,076
What kind of goddamn senior
steals money from their junior?

418
00:32:46,096 --> 00:32:47,946
You can talk to my lawyer after this.

419
00:32:49,376 --> 00:32:51,156
Are you threatening me with a lawyer?

420
00:32:51,576 --> 00:32:52,576
I'm not.

421
00:32:52,966 --> 00:32:54,576
But if you keep acting like this,

422
00:32:54,596 --> 00:32:55,836
then you're going to jail.

423
00:32:57,346 --> 00:32:58,236
- F*ck you!
- Ow!

424
00:32:59,596 --> 00:33:00,956
- Nan... Nan!
- Nan!

425
00:33:00,976 --> 00:33:02,136
Have you lost your mind?!

426
00:33:02,206 --> 00:33:04,056
- Nan, don't!
- Let go of me!

427
00:33:06,966 --> 00:33:07,756
Nadear...

428
00:33:18,296 --> 00:33:19,486
Is it really just a sprain?

429
00:33:19,506 --> 00:33:22,276
You're not lying to me about
having a fracture, are you?

430
00:33:22,496 --> 00:33:25,266
No, it's just a sprained ankle.

431
00:33:25,496 --> 00:33:27,166
Don't worry.

432
00:33:36,886 --> 00:33:37,886
Yes, Wawah?

433
00:33:37,916 --> 00:33:39,986
Are you with Nadear?

434
00:33:43,486 --> 00:33:44,776
No, what is it?

435
00:33:44,806 --> 00:33:47,136
Before you got into a fight with Nan,

436
00:33:47,156 --> 00:33:48,776
I happened to hear...

437
00:33:48,796 --> 00:33:50,646
You really want me to do this?

438
00:33:50,666 --> 00:33:51,466
Yeah.

439
00:33:51,896 --> 00:33:53,486
Push me as hard as you can.

440
00:33:53,676 --> 00:33:55,146
Are you crazy?

441
00:33:55,166 --> 00:33:55,956
Why would I push you?

442
00:33:56,186 --> 00:33:58,346
If you want this to end,
you have to do it.

443
00:34:01,286 --> 00:34:04,266
I even saw Nadear taking
spoiled milk home once.

444
00:34:04,376 --> 00:34:06,466
Probably for watering her plants.

445
00:34:07,666 --> 00:34:09,186
This is the first time

446
00:34:10,686 --> 00:34:13,076
I don't want to feel better.

447
00:34:20,976 --> 00:34:21,776
Chris.

448
00:34:33,186 --> 00:34:36,666
My parents are asking if
you can take care of me for a while.

449
00:34:36,696 --> 00:34:38,806
If you can't, they'll take care of me themselves.

450
00:34:41,036 --> 00:34:42,066
Of course,

451
00:34:42,956 --> 00:34:44,596
I'll take care of you.

452
00:34:47,716 --> 00:34:49,176
See?

453
00:34:49,566 --> 00:34:52,576
Chris can take care of me.
You don't have to worry.

454
00:34:56,676 --> 00:34:58,866
[Pork congee]

455
00:34:59,666 --> 00:35:01,276
Nadear hurt herself?!

456
00:35:04,386 --> 00:35:05,776
Yeah...

457
00:35:06,026 --> 00:35:09,236
I think she did it to keep me close,

458
00:35:09,986 --> 00:35:13,436
so I was afraid she might hurt you too.

459
00:35:14,576 --> 00:35:17,686
I really didn't send you that cheesecake.

460
00:35:19,776 --> 00:35:22,596
I sent the cake to my friend
to have it tested for contaminants.

461
00:35:22,866 --> 00:35:24,486
The results should be out soon.

462
00:35:28,086 --> 00:35:29,086
Okay.

463
00:35:36,876 --> 00:35:37,876
Chris...

464
00:35:39,706 --> 00:35:42,166
Aside from Nadear hurting herself,

465
00:35:43,156 --> 00:35:44,766
are you sure

466
00:35:45,286 --> 00:35:47,286
that what you're doing isn't hurting her too?

467
00:35:51,696 --> 00:35:53,196
I understand

468
00:35:53,696 --> 00:35:56,476
that you're taking care of her as a friend.

469
00:35:58,286 --> 00:35:59,886
I'm not saying this because I'm jealous,

470
00:36:01,286 --> 00:36:03,386
but I'm worried about you.

471
00:36:09,466 --> 00:36:11,176
Are you saying that...

472
00:36:11,686 --> 00:36:12,966
what I'm doing

473
00:36:12,986 --> 00:36:15,306
is still giving Nadear false hope?

474
00:36:17,286 --> 00:36:19,486
Don't you think so?

475
00:36:21,616 --> 00:36:23,066
Ow!

476
00:36:24,526 --> 00:36:25,296
Nadear.

477
00:36:26,576 --> 00:36:28,076
Nadear, are you okay?

478
00:36:28,576 --> 00:36:29,876
Can I come in?

479
00:36:30,676 --> 00:36:31,996
Go ahead.

480
00:36:34,606 --> 00:36:35,756
Is everything alright?

481
00:36:35,976 --> 00:36:37,866
It's so hard to shower.

482
00:36:38,766 --> 00:36:40,356
Can you help me?

483
00:36:44,896 --> 00:36:47,086
Here, this should make it easier now.

484
00:36:47,106 --> 00:36:49,246
I told you I'd take care of you.

485
00:36:51,786 --> 00:36:53,636
You're such a good friend, huh?

486
00:36:54,096 --> 00:36:54,886
Yeah,

487
00:36:54,916 --> 00:36:56,776
I'll be a good friend to you.

488
00:36:57,176 --> 00:36:59,446
Hurry and shower before
you catch a cold, okay?

489
00:36:59,466 --> 00:37:00,576
I'm leaving now.

490
00:37:03,286 --> 00:37:04,186
Chris.

491
00:37:04,206 --> 00:37:06,066
Chris, where are you going?!

492
00:37:22,776 --> 00:37:24,796
When a friend pours you water,

493
00:37:25,376 --> 00:37:26,466
you don't think much of it.

494
00:37:27,986 --> 00:37:29,856
But if it's someone you like,

495
00:37:30,196 --> 00:37:31,486
even pouring you water

496
00:37:32,686 --> 00:37:34,496
can feel special.

497
00:37:41,776 --> 00:37:43,776
When a friend shares something
they like with you,

498
00:37:44,596 --> 00:37:45,976
you just see it as a kind gesture.

499
00:37:47,176 --> 00:37:49,286
But when someone you like does it,

500
00:37:50,386 --> 00:37:51,886
you assume they like you back.

501
00:37:55,886 --> 00:37:56,886
Mm.

502
00:37:57,366 --> 00:37:58,846
The same action...

503
00:37:58,866 --> 00:37:59,946
but seen differently.

504
00:38:06,286 --> 00:38:07,176
Oh no.

505
00:38:07,856 --> 00:38:09,376
What will she think

506
00:38:10,176 --> 00:38:11,806
if I bathe her?

507
00:38:12,176 --> 00:38:12,966
Chris?!

508
00:38:15,726 --> 00:38:17,236
It's nothing...

509
00:38:17,256 --> 00:38:18,596
Nadear just asked me for help,

510
00:38:18,616 --> 00:38:19,876
so I helped her.

511
00:38:20,896 --> 00:38:21,976
Should you be doing that?

512
00:38:27,956 --> 00:38:30,316
This is far worse than giving false hope.

513
00:38:30,646 --> 00:38:31,896
Whoa, whoa, uh...

514
00:38:34,336 --> 00:38:35,186
Is this

515
00:38:35,526 --> 00:38:37,446
what you call being jealous?

516
00:38:42,316 --> 00:38:43,576
You still have to ask that?

517
00:38:44,556 --> 00:38:46,466
If Nadear hurts herself again,

518
00:38:46,796 --> 00:38:48,366
just know that it's because of you.

519
00:38:50,686 --> 00:38:52,766
Just kidding.

520
00:38:52,916 --> 00:38:55,496
I just don't want to see
you looking sad anymore.

521
00:38:55,936 --> 00:38:58,356
I want to see your grumpy face, too.

522
00:39:03,816 --> 00:39:06,746
If I know what upsets you,

523
00:39:07,666 --> 00:39:09,276
I won't do it.

524
00:39:13,476 --> 00:39:14,696
Because...

525
00:39:15,096 --> 00:39:17,576
I've already upset you enough.

526
00:39:26,186 --> 00:39:26,776
Here.

527
00:39:27,516 --> 00:39:29,436
Eat up, baby.

528
00:39:30,126 --> 00:39:32,196
I give you this because

529
00:39:32,216 --> 00:39:34,356
I care about you and love you.

530
00:39:36,076 --> 00:39:37,406
What's with the "baby"?

531
00:39:37,686 --> 00:39:38,686
You idiot.

532
00:39:39,686 --> 00:39:40,646
Aha,

533
00:39:40,666 --> 00:39:42,416
you liked that, didn't you?

534
00:39:42,436 --> 00:39:43,556
Look at you smiling.

535
00:39:49,536 --> 00:39:51,556
Don't be sad.

536
00:39:52,466 --> 00:39:53,466
Eat this too.

537
00:39:55,766 --> 00:39:57,466
Here's the dish.

538
00:40:09,806 --> 00:40:11,106
Aren't we getting out together?

539
00:40:14,166 --> 00:40:17,626
I forgot we can't go public yet.

540
00:40:18,556 --> 00:40:21,396
I'd rather you spend time with your friend.

541
00:40:21,426 --> 00:40:23,866
And there are doctors
looking to invest in your business, too.

542
00:40:24,986 --> 00:40:27,996
But if you want to go public,
I can get out with you now.

543
00:40:28,676 --> 00:40:29,686
It's okay.

544
00:40:30,626 --> 00:40:33,186
You cared about my friend,

545
00:40:33,686 --> 00:40:36,376
so I'll care about your friend, too.

546
00:40:37,276 --> 00:40:37,806
But...

547
00:40:38,966 --> 00:40:40,206
just friends, okay?

548
00:40:42,686 --> 00:40:43,186
Yeah.

549
00:40:44,176 --> 00:40:45,106
Then...

550
00:40:45,496 --> 00:40:46,976
I won't look forward to helping
my friend take a bath anymore.

551
00:40:48,096 --> 00:40:50,186
I'll only look forward to
helping my girlfriend take a bath.

552
00:40:55,576 --> 00:40:56,266
Wait.

553
00:40:59,726 --> 00:41:00,376
Here.

554
00:41:01,256 --> 00:41:02,476
In case you feel cold, Doc.

555
00:41:05,596 --> 00:41:06,676
Thank you.

556
00:41:07,526 --> 00:41:09,076
If you want to go home, call me, okay?

557
00:41:09,186 --> 00:41:09,976
I'll come pick you up.

558
00:41:09,996 --> 00:41:10,516
Mm.

559
00:41:11,186 --> 00:41:12,186
Okay.

560
00:41:13,406 --> 00:41:14,586
- Bye-bye.
- Bye-bye.

561
00:41:33,766 --> 00:41:35,346
Where is Air?

562
00:41:36,196 --> 00:41:37,586
She's on her way.

563
00:41:41,366 --> 00:41:42,006
Oh,

564
00:41:42,776 --> 00:41:44,376
there are clinics everywhere,

565
00:41:44,396 --> 00:41:46,376
so why do they want to invest in us?

566
00:41:46,826 --> 00:41:47,996
I don't know either.

567
00:41:48,506 --> 00:41:50,866
But... I want Air as a shareholder,

568
00:41:51,166 --> 00:41:52,576
'cause she's pretty.

569
00:41:52,786 --> 00:41:53,786
Ugh.

570
00:41:54,696 --> 00:41:55,696
No wonder

571
00:41:55,716 --> 00:41:57,346
you asked her to meet up here.

572
00:41:57,366 --> 00:41:58,666
You plan to get her drunk, huh?

573
00:41:58,846 --> 00:42:00,156
Are you crazy?

574
00:42:04,166 --> 00:42:05,196
She called me.

575
00:42:08,886 --> 00:42:10,166
Hello, Air?

576
00:42:10,736 --> 00:42:12,286
Oh, you're here?

577
00:42:12,586 --> 00:42:14,476
I'm at the bar with my friend.

578
00:42:19,886 --> 00:42:21,386
Is that pretty woman

579
00:42:21,776 --> 00:42:23,186
Air?

580
00:42:24,576 --> 00:42:25,576
Yeah.

581
00:42:31,486 --> 00:42:32,996
So why...

582
00:42:33,076 --> 00:42:34,786
is Aek with her?

583
00:42:40,436 --> 00:42:41,576
I didn't know...

584
00:42:41,596 --> 00:42:43,946
Air knew your ex.

585
00:42:49,986 --> 00:42:51,296
- Hello, Air.
- Hello.

586
00:42:51,316 --> 00:42:52,226
Hello.

587
00:42:52,246 --> 00:42:53,506
Hello.

588
00:43:09,306 --> 00:43:12,066
Sa-run is also interested
in your skin clinic,

589
00:43:12,446 --> 00:43:14,186
so I brought him here.

590
00:43:15,036 --> 00:43:16,456
I just found out...

591
00:43:16,916 --> 00:43:18,686
you two already know each other.

592
00:43:18,876 --> 00:43:20,066
It's a small world, huh?

593
00:43:25,076 --> 00:43:26,376
Um, one second.

594
00:43:28,606 --> 00:43:30,036
Hello?

595
00:43:30,386 --> 00:43:32,166
Yes, I'll be there soon.

596
00:43:34,776 --> 00:43:35,556
Uh...

597
00:43:36,086 --> 00:43:37,086
I...

598
00:43:37,266 --> 00:43:39,086
have an urgent case.

599
00:43:39,316 --> 00:43:42,546
Can we meet up again some other time?

600
00:43:42,766 --> 00:43:44,356
Oh, let me walk you out.

601
00:43:44,606 --> 00:43:45,396
Okay.

602
00:43:45,806 --> 00:43:46,856
See you later.

603
00:43:46,896 --> 00:43:48,036
I'll be right back.

604
00:43:48,956 --> 00:43:49,876
It won't take long.

605
00:43:54,376 --> 00:43:55,706
Since when did you come back?

606
00:43:56,286 --> 00:43:57,776
Why haven't I heard about this?

607
00:43:59,066 --> 00:44:00,386
I missed you, Sun.

608
00:44:01,776 --> 00:44:03,366
What is there to miss?

609
00:44:03,876 --> 00:44:05,266
We only dated for two months.

610
00:44:05,666 --> 00:44:06,766
We met a few times

611
00:44:07,296 --> 00:44:08,356
before we broke up.

612
00:44:09,956 --> 00:44:11,646
Well, other than my family,

613
00:44:12,356 --> 00:44:13,356
you're the only one

614
00:44:13,686 --> 00:44:14,786
who calls me Aek.

615
00:44:15,796 --> 00:44:16,946
Perhaps I missed you

616
00:44:16,966 --> 00:44:17,966
because of that.

617
00:44:19,096 --> 00:44:20,366
Don't you think

618
00:44:20,806 --> 00:44:22,666
we ended things a bit too abruptly?

619
00:44:23,826 --> 00:44:24,676
You know

620
00:44:24,696 --> 00:44:26,266
why we dated back then.

621
00:44:26,296 --> 00:44:28,576
I let you use me
to make other people jealous,

622
00:44:29,786 --> 00:44:31,176
but I actually love you now.

623
00:44:33,046 --> 00:44:34,046
To be honest,

624
00:44:35,706 --> 00:44:36,876
I've always had feelings for you.

625
00:44:46,496 --> 00:44:50,766
[I'll be back soon.
Air is still waiting for her ride]

626
00:44:54,036 --> 00:44:55,276
We should meet up another time

627
00:44:55,786 --> 00:44:57,086
since we're not all here anyway.

628
00:44:58,946 --> 00:45:00,686
But I want to talk to you about something.

629
00:45:02,276 --> 00:45:03,586
Did you like the cheesecake?

630
00:45:05,896 --> 00:45:06,976
Cheesecake?

631
00:45:08,626 --> 00:45:09,796
Did you send that to me?

632
00:45:09,816 --> 00:45:10,956
It's delicious, wasn't it?

633
00:45:11,586 --> 00:45:13,466
How did you know I like cheesecake?

634
00:45:14,216 --> 00:45:16,366
Why didn't you tell me you sent it?

635
00:45:16,386 --> 00:45:18,066
How did you know where I work?

636
00:45:19,576 --> 00:45:20,576
Calm down.

637
00:45:21,976 --> 00:45:23,966
I knew I'd see you soon,

638
00:45:24,396 --> 00:45:25,786
so I wanted to surprise you.

639
00:45:27,716 --> 00:45:30,156
Who told you I like cheesecake?

640
00:45:31,406 --> 00:45:33,056
If you want to know,

641
00:45:34,976 --> 00:45:36,486
then have a few more drinks with me.

642
00:45:52,556 --> 00:45:55,386
Things aren't great right now.

643
00:45:55,406 --> 00:45:57,076
Can you come pick me up?

644
00:46:01,986 --> 00:46:05,176
[Third Person]

645
00:46:06,417 --> 00:46:10,207
[Third Person]

646
00:46:14,617 --> 00:46:15,767
When are you going to tell me

647
00:46:15,907 --> 00:46:17,407
who told you?

648
00:46:17,727 --> 00:46:18,997
No one told me.

649
00:46:20,427 --> 00:46:21,427
I just...

650
00:46:21,727 --> 00:46:22,727
guessed.

651
00:46:25,777 --> 00:46:27,327
How could you guess my address right?

652
00:46:27,757 --> 00:46:29,117
Don't lie to me.

653
00:46:29,557 --> 00:46:31,427
I know this isn't a coincidence.

654
00:46:31,727 --> 00:46:32,907
Tonight, too.

655
00:46:42,727 --> 00:46:43,387
Yes.

656
00:46:45,247 --> 00:46:46,897
I knew you were back,

657
00:46:48,087 --> 00:46:49,697
so I came to see you.

658
00:46:55,397 --> 00:46:57,507
I really want us to get back together.

659
00:46:59,297 --> 00:47:01,427
If you really want us to get back together,

660
00:47:01,637 --> 00:47:02,707
you'll have to tell me

661
00:47:02,727 --> 00:47:03,907
who told you.

662
00:47:18,887 --> 00:47:20,087
My junior,

663
00:47:21,817 --> 00:47:22,817
Nadear.

664
00:47:25,517 --> 00:47:27,107
You know her, don't you?

665
00:47:28,147 --> 00:47:30,497
She asked me about you

666
00:47:30,577 --> 00:47:32,027
four years ago

667
00:47:32,047 --> 00:47:33,537
when you had an accident.

668
00:47:38,177 --> 00:47:39,177
Where are you going?

669
00:47:39,197 --> 00:47:39,897
Sun.

670
00:47:41,827 --> 00:47:42,827
Would you like the check now?

671
00:47:47,997 --> 00:47:48,997
I'm sorry!

672
00:47:50,947 --> 00:47:52,217
Let's exchange IGs,

673
00:47:52,647 --> 00:47:53,807
and I'll forgive you.

674
00:47:54,917 --> 00:47:56,797
I'm not interested, sorry.

675
00:47:57,097 --> 00:47:58,227
Wait.

676
00:47:58,247 --> 00:47:59,567
Playing hard to get, huh?

677
00:48:00,017 --> 00:48:01,397
It's just your IG.

678
00:48:01,617 --> 00:48:02,997
Why are you being so cold?

679
00:48:03,807 --> 00:48:05,167
I'm sorry, but no.

680
00:48:05,187 --> 00:48:06,497
What's the rush?

681
00:48:06,517 --> 00:48:07,687
Let go, please.

682
00:48:12,637 --> 00:48:14,517
She said no. Don't you get it?

683
00:48:14,877 --> 00:48:16,007
Or do I have to call the police?

684
00:48:18,297 --> 00:48:18,827
Chris...

685
00:48:20,367 --> 00:48:22,317
Oh...

686
00:48:22,547 --> 00:48:24,617
A jealous friend.

687
00:48:25,627 --> 00:48:26,727
Not her friend.

688
00:48:29,977 --> 00:48:30,487
Girlfriend.

689
00:48:34,607 --> 00:48:35,417
That's right.

690
00:48:35,867 --> 00:48:36,517
Girlfriend.

691
00:48:37,327 --> 00:48:38,327
Goodbye now.

692
00:48:45,217 --> 00:48:46,307
You got here so fast.

693
00:48:47,207 --> 00:48:48,707
I'm here to pick up a drunk girl.

694
00:48:49,007 --> 00:48:50,007
How drunk are you?

695
00:48:50,217 --> 00:48:51,327
Just a little.

696
00:48:52,107 --> 00:48:53,177
Come on, let's go home.

697
00:48:53,197 --> 00:48:54,007
Mm.

698
00:48:55,627 --> 00:48:56,627
Oh, Chris.

699
00:49:01,477 --> 00:49:02,727
Isn't Nadear with you?

700
00:49:08,107 --> 00:49:09,107
No, she isn't.

701
00:49:09,977 --> 00:49:12,607
I met Nadear's parents a few days ago.

702
00:49:13,407 --> 00:49:14,407
They said you

703
00:49:14,437 --> 00:49:15,777
and Nadear are going to get married.

704
00:49:18,567 --> 00:49:19,807
Don't forget to invite me, too.

705
00:49:22,717 --> 00:49:23,407
Yes.

706
00:49:29,427 --> 00:49:30,427
Sun, I'll drive you home.

707
00:49:30,447 --> 00:49:31,297
No need.

708
00:49:31,427 --> 00:49:32,427
I'll drive her home.

709
00:49:48,347 --> 00:49:49,707
How can we get back together

710
00:49:50,917 --> 00:49:52,617
if you don't take care of your girl?

711
00:49:53,727 --> 00:49:55,527
Chris came to take Sun home.

712
00:50:10,127 --> 00:50:12,277
[I bought this for you, Nadear]

713
00:50:23,157 --> 00:50:24,157
Are you cold?

714
00:50:28,317 --> 00:50:30,517
I'm sorry for upsetting you.

715
00:50:30,817 --> 00:50:33,687
Sa-run is close to Nadear's parents.

716
00:50:34,297 --> 00:50:35,767
I'm sorry

717
00:50:36,237 --> 00:50:37,847
for getting upset

718
00:50:38,247 --> 00:50:41,537
when I'm supposed to be
someone you can feel at ease with.

719
00:50:42,017 --> 00:50:43,387
You always have been,

720
00:50:44,627 --> 00:50:45,627
until earlier.

721
00:50:49,667 --> 00:50:52,007
I shouldn't have left you alone.

722
00:50:52,677 --> 00:50:54,627
Just thinking that something
bad might happen to you

723
00:50:54,647 --> 00:50:56,197
makes my heart sink.

724
00:50:57,337 --> 00:50:58,337
That's right.

725
00:50:59,177 --> 00:51:01,207
I fell in love with you

726
00:51:02,507 --> 00:51:05,207
who always protect others.

727
00:51:06,967 --> 00:51:07,697
Hm?

728
00:51:10,517 --> 00:51:12,407
Well...what I mean is,

729
00:51:12,707 --> 00:51:13,797
I'm alright now.

730
00:51:14,097 --> 00:51:16,007
I have you here with me.

731
00:51:19,917 --> 00:51:22,077
Oh, when you said

732
00:51:22,097 --> 00:51:23,697
things weren't great,

733
00:51:24,357 --> 00:51:26,547
was it because of Sa-run?

734
00:51:26,927 --> 00:51:27,927
Mm...

735
00:51:28,777 --> 00:51:31,177
Aek was the one who sent
me that cheesecake,

736
00:51:32,347 --> 00:51:33,897
but at least it wasn't Nadear's doing.

737
00:51:34,517 --> 00:51:36,507
She didn't mean to hurt anyone,

738
00:51:37,747 --> 00:51:39,087
only herself.

739
00:51:39,507 --> 00:51:40,797
That's a relief.

740
00:51:42,677 --> 00:51:43,417
It's not.

741
00:51:44,627 --> 00:51:45,627
Why?

742
00:51:47,397 --> 00:51:48,327
I'm jealous.

743
00:51:58,307 --> 00:51:59,307
You can be jealous,

744
00:51:59,997 --> 00:52:01,207
but don't stress too much.

745
00:52:03,027 --> 00:52:05,507
Because you're the only one

746
00:52:06,917 --> 00:52:08,707
I have feelings for, Chris.

747
00:52:15,067 --> 00:52:16,807
Okay.

748
00:52:17,147 --> 00:52:19,247
We should go home.

749
00:52:20,007 --> 00:52:21,237
Because

750
00:52:21,257 --> 00:52:22,157
your girlfriend here

751
00:52:22,177 --> 00:52:24,547
is going to give you a bath as a reward.

752
00:52:25,067 --> 00:52:26,287
Chris!

753
00:52:26,367 --> 00:52:27,287
Are you crazy?

754
00:52:27,657 --> 00:52:28,727
You don't want to?

755
00:52:29,527 --> 00:52:30,027
Hm?

756
00:52:31,587 --> 00:52:32,927
Come on, let's go home.

757
00:52:32,957 --> 00:52:34,597
Let's go.

758
00:52:34,907 --> 00:52:35,697
Let's go home.

759
00:53:05,807 --> 00:53:07,407
How did you know my size?

760
00:53:10,197 --> 00:53:11,497
How could I not?

761
00:53:23,707 --> 00:53:25,467
Hm, come here.

762
00:53:26,857 --> 00:53:27,807
Are you cold?

763
00:53:28,347 --> 00:53:29,127
I'm okay.

764
00:53:29,827 --> 00:53:32,197
Why...did you bring me here?

765
00:53:32,217 --> 00:53:33,677
Weren't we going home?

766
00:53:37,497 --> 00:53:40,357
Well, you said you wanted to swim
when we went to the beach,

767
00:53:40,697 --> 00:53:42,097
but I had to go back first.

768
00:53:43,127 --> 00:53:45,407
So I brought you here to swim today.

769
00:53:47,217 --> 00:53:48,227
Thank you

770
00:53:48,987 --> 00:53:51,087
for remembering I wanted to swim.

771
00:53:53,897 --> 00:53:54,897
Actually...

772
00:53:57,227 --> 00:53:58,907
I want to do something else as well.

773
00:54:03,197 --> 00:54:03,897
What is it?

774
00:54:11,827 --> 00:54:12,827
Can I say it?

775
00:54:16,177 --> 00:54:18,077
If you don't say it,

776
00:54:19,207 --> 00:54:20,517
I'll do it myself.

777
00:54:25,717 --> 00:54:26,907
Say it again.

778
00:54:28,807 --> 00:54:29,807
Say what?

779
00:54:31,747 --> 00:54:33,497
Say that I'm your "girlfriend."

780
00:54:38,807 --> 00:54:44,117
♫Like the sunlight♫

781
00:54:44,297 --> 00:54:46,557
♫Providing warm embrace♫

782
00:54:46,577 --> 00:54:50,147
♫Always being near, hugging you tight,♫

783
00:54:50,177 --> 00:54:54,197
♫So you don't shed a tear♫

784
00:55:00,867 --> 00:55:02,387
Can you do it for me, girlfriend?

785
00:55:02,927 --> 00:55:04,657
♫When you look up high♫

786
00:55:04,677 --> 00:55:08,167
♫The Sun will be there, shining in the sky♫

787
00:55:08,387 --> 00:55:11,127
♫'Cause I'm your SUN♫

788
00:55:11,147 --> 00:55:14,857
♫I'll be your sun, you'll be my sky♫

789
00:55:14,877 --> 00:55:18,607
♫I'll be your sun, you'll be my sky♫

790
00:55:18,627 --> 00:55:20,677
♫When you look up high♫

791
00:55:20,707 --> 00:55:24,407
♫The Sun will be there, shining in the sky♫

792
00:55:24,427 --> 00:55:27,747
♫'Cause I'm your SUN♫

793
00:55:27,777 --> 00:55:34,697
♫If you have to face the storm,
once the rain goes by♫

794
00:55:34,727 --> 00:55:36,457
♫When you look up high♫

795
00:55:36,477 --> 00:55:40,287
♫The Sun will be there, shining in the sky♫

796
00:55:40,307 --> 00:55:43,227
♫'Cause I'm your SUN♫

797
00:55:43,247 --> 00:55:46,427
♫I'll be your sun, you'll be my sky♫

798
00:56:02,827 --> 00:56:04,307
Why is it so hard?

799
00:56:13,647 --> 00:56:16,207
[Chris]

800
00:56:38,367 --> 00:56:40,557
[How to make a flower ring]

801
00:56:45,027 --> 00:56:46,077
[Chris]

802
00:56:52,317 --> 00:56:53,187
Chris,

803
00:56:53,897 --> 00:56:55,597
how do I make a flower ring?

804
00:56:56,997 --> 00:56:57,837
Sun,

805
00:57:00,887 --> 00:57:02,307
can we meet?

806
00:57:09,647 --> 00:57:11,507
We haven't seen each other in a long time.

807
00:57:16,007 --> 00:57:17,217
Why are you back?

808
00:57:24,117 --> 00:57:26,207
It's been years,

809
00:57:26,317 --> 00:57:28,297
and you're still just as selfish, huh?

810
00:57:29,607 --> 00:57:31,217
Stop bothering Chris already.

811
00:57:32,007 --> 00:57:33,207
I'm sorry.

812
00:57:34,197 --> 00:57:35,527
I can't do that.

813
00:57:35,997 --> 00:57:37,297
I love Chris.

814
00:57:41,747 --> 00:57:43,417
Only for now.

815
00:57:44,617 --> 00:57:47,717
Once Chris learns what you did,

816
00:57:48,047 --> 00:57:49,127
do you really think

817
00:57:50,537 --> 00:57:52,427
she'll still love you?

818
00:57:53,807 --> 00:57:55,597
Chris will leave you

819
00:57:56,727 --> 00:57:58,187
just like you left her.

820
00:58:26,117 --> 00:58:27,407
I know everything now.

821
00:58:29,177 --> 00:58:30,707
Let's end things here.

822
00:58:39,497 --> 00:58:40,767
You still cared?

823
00:58:40,797 --> 00:58:42,407
If you enjoy playing the victim,

824
00:58:42,607 --> 00:58:44,567
then don't try to make me
the villain, Nadear.

825
00:58:44,587 --> 00:58:46,417
You can say whatever you want to me,

826
00:58:46,437 --> 00:58:47,177
but don't say

827
00:58:47,567 --> 00:58:48,917
that you have no one left.

828
00:58:51,127 --> 00:58:53,117
I won't make the same mistake again.

829
00:58:54,857 --> 00:58:55,567
Sun!

830
00:58:56,287 --> 00:58:57,727
The truth between you and Sun.

831
00:58:57,927 --> 00:58:58,927
What truth?

832
00:58:59,057 --> 00:59:01,287
Our relationship was wrong
from the beginning.

833
00:59:18,007 --> 00:59:27,927
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

834
